<?php elseif($page==='att_upload'&&academic($user)):?><section class="card"><h2>Upload Teaching Timetable</h2><p>Enrolled tutors can edit their own future flexible sessions at <a href="my-research-timetable.php">My flexible teaching sessions</a>.</p><div class="service-links"><a class="button" href="?page=att_new">Enter class timetable manually</a><a class="button secondary" href="?page=att_template">Download Excel template</a><a class="button secondary" href="?page=att_csv_template">Download CSV template</a></div><p>Department in the file means the department receiving the class; tutors may teach outside their home department. For combined classes, use one row per participating group with the same Combined Session ID and identical tutor, module, date/day, time and room. They become one attendance session. Use different IDs for separate sessions. Student Count is the optional total across all groups. For occasional research classes, fill Class Date with the actual teaching date. Repeat the same tutor and module on separate rows for Monday, Wednesday or any other teaching day. Leave Class Date blank for weekly classes. All academic year, semester, date and timing details must be filled in the file.</p><p>The Excel template includes an Instructions sheet with examples and a Settings sheet with the Admin-configured calendar and timings. The first Timetable sheet is where you enter your real classes.</p><form method="post" enctype="multipart/form-data"><?php csrf();?><input type="hidden" name="action" value="att_upload"><?php field('sheet','Upload Excel or CSV','file');?><button>Validate and preview</button></form></section><?php require __DIR__.'/import-history.php';?><?php if(isset($_SESSION['att_import'])):$items=$_SESSION['att_import'];$valid=count(array_filter($items,fn($i)=>$i['status']==='Valid'));?><section class="card"><h2>Upload Preview</h2><p>Total <?=count($items)?> · Valid <?=$valid?> · Errors <?=count($items)-$valid?> · Warnings 0</p><a href="?page=att_errors">Download error report</a><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Row</th><th>Tutor</th><th>Subject</th><th>Room</th><th>Time</th><th>Status / message</th></tr></thead><tbody><?php foreach($items as $item):$r=$item['source'];?><tr><td><?=$item['row']?></td><td><?=e($r['Tutor Email']??'')?></td><td><?=e($r['Subject Name']??'')?></td><td><?=e($r['Classroom']??'')?></td><td><?=e(($r['Start Time']??'').'–'.($r['End Time']??''))?></td><td><?=e($item['status'].' '.$item['message'])?></td></tr><?php endforeach;?></tbody></table></div><p>Only the valid rows listed above will be imported. Correct and upload error rows separately.</p><?php if($valid):attForm('att_import');?><button>Import <?=$valid?> Valid Records</button></form><?php endif;attForm('att_cancel_import');?><button class="secondary">Cancel preview</button></form></section><?php endif;?>
